    <div class="card">
      <h2>Activity Sheet Solutions</h2>

      <ol>
        <li><strong>Simple annuity:</strong> Equal payments are made at equal intervals, and the payment interval coincides with the interest-conversion interval.</li>

        <li><strong>General annuity:</strong> The payment interval and interest-conversion interval are different.</li>

        <li><strong>Deferred annuity:</strong> Payments begin only after a stated waiting period.</li>

        <li><strong>Ordinary annuity:</strong> Payments are made at the end of each period.</li>

        <li>
          <strong>Given:</strong> R = ₱3,000, nominal rate = 6%, monthly compounding, time = 2 years.<br>
          i = 0.06 ÷ 12 = 0.005<br>
          n = 2 × 12 = 24<br>
          FV = R[(1 + i)ⁿ − 1] ÷ i<br>
          FV = ₱3,000[(1.005)²⁴ − 1] ÷ 0.005<br>
          <strong>FV ≈ ₱76,295.87</strong><br>
          This is a simple annuity because both payment and conversion intervals are monthly.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Given:</strong> R = ₱2,000, i = 0.06 ÷ 12 = 0.005, n = 18.<br>
          FV = ₱2,000[(1.005)¹⁸ − 1] ÷ 0.005<br>
          <strong>FV ≈ ₱37,571.58</strong>
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> General annuity.<br>
          Payment interval = quarterly.<br>
          Interest-conversion interval = monthly.<br>
          Because the intervals differ, it is a general annuity.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Given:</strong> R = ₱4,000, nominal rate = 6%, quarterly compounding, time = 3 years.<br>
          i = 0.06 ÷ 4 = 0.015<br>
          n = 3 × 4 = 12<br>
          FV = ₱4,000[(1.015)¹² − 1] ÷ 0.015<br>
          <strong>FV ≈ ₱52,164.85</strong>
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> Deferred annuity.<br>
          The payments begin only after a six-month waiting period.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Comparison:</strong><br>
          Simple = matching payment and interest-conversion intervals.<br>
          General = different payment and interest-conversion intervals.<br>
          Deferred = payments begin after a waiting period.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> General annuity.<br>
          Payment interval = six months.<br>
          Interest-conversion interval = three months.<br>
          The intervals differ.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Given:</strong> R = ₱1,500, nominal rate = 12%, monthly compounding, time = 12 months.<br>
          i = 0.12 ÷ 12 = 0.01<br>
          n = 12<br>
          FV = ₱1,500[(1.01)¹² − 1] ÷ 0.01<br>
          <strong>FV ≈ ₱19,023.75</strong>
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> The statement is incorrect.<br>
          Regular payments alone do not make an annuity simple. The payment interval must also coincide with the interest-conversion interval. Quarterly payments with monthly compounding therefore describe a general annuity.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Acceptable answer:</strong> A retirement or investment plan in which regular benefits begin after a waiting period. It is deferred because the first payment does not begin immediately.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Given:</strong> R = ₱5,000, nominal rate = 8%, quarterly compounding, time = 2 years.<br>
          i = 0.08 ÷ 4 = 0.02<br>
          n = 2 × 4 = 8<br>
          FV = ₱5,000[(1.02)⁸ − 1] ÷ 0.02<br>
          <strong>FV ≈ ₱42,914.85</strong><br>
          Interpretation: after the stated period, the accumulated value of the regular deposits is approximately ₱42,914.85.
        </li>
      </ol>
